  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow" style="display: block; margin-bottom: 24px;">Trust Framework</span>
      <h1>
        Trust is architecture,<br>
        <span class="text-accent">not a marketing claim.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="hero-subheadline" style="max-width: 720px; margin: 24px auto 0;">
        In institutional environments, trust must be demonstrated through system design — not assumed through reputation. ROUAA's trust is not a claim — it is the property of a system
        whose outputs can be reconstructed, verified, and defended. This page documents the four architectural pillars
        that produce that property.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="background: var(--rouaa-bg-secondary);" id="definition">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header text-center" style="margin: 0 auto 48px;">
        <span class="eyebrow">What Trust Means At ROUAA</span>
        <h2>A decision is "trusted" only if it can be reconstructed.</h2>
        <p style="margin: 0 auto; max-width: 720px;">
          A decision supported by ROUAA intelligence is defensible not because ROUAA says so — but because the decision itself carries
          the full chain of evidence, governance, and reasoning that produced it. Any auditor, any committee member,
          any regulator can follow the chain from decision back to source document. That reconstructability is what
          we call trust.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-3" style="max-width: 1040px; margin: 0 auto;">
        <div class="card">
          <h4 style="margin-bottom: 12px; color: var(--rouaa-accent);">Trust ≠ Claim</h4>
          <p style="font-size: 14px;">"Trusted by institutions" is a claim. Reconstructable evidence chains are trust. ROUAA produces the evidence infrastructure that allows institutions to verify decisions themselves.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h4 style="margin-bottom: 12px; color: var(--rouaa-accent);">Trust ≠ Speed</h4>
          <p style="font-size: 14px;">Fast outputs are not necessarily trusted outputs. ROUAA optimizes for the combination — speed through automation, trust through governance.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h4 style="margin-bottom: 12px; color: var(--rouaa-accent);">Trust ≠ Volume</h4>
          <p style="font-size: 14px;">More data does not equal more trust. The right data, with the right provenance, governed by the right rules — that is what produces defensible outputs.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="pillars">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header text-center" style="margin: 0 auto 48px;">
        <span class="eyebrow">The Four Pillars</span>
        <h2>Four architectural pillars of the Trust Framework.</h2>
        <p style="margin: 0 auto; max-width: 680px;">Each pillar is a structural property of the system — not a feature, not a policy, not a marketing message.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-2" style="max-width: 1040px; margin: 0 auto; gap: 24px;">
        <div class="card" style="border-top: 3px solid var(--rouaa-accent);">
          <h4 style="margin-bottom: 8px; color: var(--rouaa-text-muted); font-size: 13px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em;">Pillar 01</h4>
          <h3 style="margin-bottom: 16px; color: var(--rouaa-accent); font-size: 22px;">Evidence Provenance</h3>
          <p style="font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 16px;">Intelligence outputs generated through ROUAA workflows inherit their full provenance chain — the source document, the page, the paragraph, the extraction confidence, the governance validation.</p>
          <div style="border-top: 1px solid var(--rouaa-surface-border); padding-top: 16px;">
            <div style="font-size: 12px; color: var(--rouaa-text-muted); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; margin-bottom: 8px;">What It Means In Practice</div>
            <p style="font-size: 13px;">If a published analysis says "the central bank raised rates by 25bps," you can click through to the press release, the paragraph, and the extraction confidence — in real time, during committee.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="card" style="border-top: 3px solid var(--rouaa-accent);">
          <h4 style="margin-bottom: 8px; color: var(--rouaa-text-muted); font-size: 13px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em;">Pillar 02</h4>
          <h3 style="margin-bottom: 16px; color: var(--rouaa-accent); font-size: 22px;">Governance By Design</h3>
          <p style="font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 16px;">Validation rules, confidence scoring, and source hierarchy operate <em>before</em> analysis is produced. Intelligence governance is structural — built into the architecture, not bolted on at the end.</p>
          <div style="border-top: 1px solid var(--rouaa-surface-border); padding-top: 16px;">
            <div style="font-size: 12px; color: var(--rouaa-text-muted); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; margin-bottom: 8px;">What It Means In Practice</div>
            <p style="font-size: 13px;">Governed intelligence systems operate only on validated intelligence inputs. Facts below confidence thresholds never reach intelligence production.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="card" style="border-top: 3px solid var(--rouaa-accent);">
          <h4 style="margin-bottom: 8px; color: var(--rouaa-text-muted); font-size: 13px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em;">Pillar 03</h4>
          <h3 style="margin-bottom: 16px; color: var(--rouaa-accent); font-size: 22px;">Decision Continuity</h3>
          <p style="font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 16px;">One infrastructure connecting source, evidence, reasoning, and institutional workflows. No silos between data, research, analysis, and execution.</p>
          <div style="border-top: 1px solid var(--rouaa-surface-border); padding-top: 16px;">
            <div style="font-size: 12px; color: var(--rouaa-text-muted); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; margin-bottom: 8px;">What It Means In Practice</div>
            <p style="font-size: 13px;">A trading decision carries the evidence chain from the analyst's research note, which carries it from the event intelligence, which carries it from the source document. End-to-end continuity.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="card" style="border-top: 3px solid var(--rouaa-accent);">
          <h4 style="margin-bottom: 8px; color: var(--rouaa-text-muted); font-size: 13px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em;">Pillar 04</h4>
          <h3 style="margin-bottom: 16px; color: var(--rouaa-accent); font-size: 22px;">Audit-Ready Output</h3>
          <p style="font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 16px;">Every output is reconstructable. Every decision, every analysis, every published claim can be traced from output back through the evidence chain to the original source — on demand, for authorized reviewers and institutional oversight teams.</p>
          <div style="border-top: 1px solid var(--rouaa-surface-border); padding-top: 16px;">
            <div style="font-size: 12px; color: var(--rouaa-text-muted); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; margin-bottom: 8px;">What It Means In Practice</div>
            <p style="font-size: 13px;">When compliance asks "how did we arrive at this position?" — the answer is not "the analyst said so." The answer is a reconstructable chain of evidence, governance, and reasoning.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="background: var(--rouaa-bg-secondary);" id="evidence-chain">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header text-center" style="margin: 0 auto 48px;">
        <span class="eyebrow">The Evidence Chain</span>
        <h2>The output contract of the Trust Framework.</h2>
        <p style="margin: 0 auto; max-width: 680px;">The evidence chain is what the four pillars produce. It is the structural property that distinguishes a ROUAA-backed decision from any other.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="max-width: 540px; margin: 0 auto; text-align: center; padding: 36px; border: 1px solid var(--rouaa-accent-border); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); background: var(--rouaa-surface); box-shadow: 0 0 32px rgba(201, 162, 39, 0.06);">
        <div style="font-size: 16px; color: var(--rouaa-text-primary); font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 8px;">Official Source</div>
        <div style="color: var(--rouaa-text-muted); margin-bottom: 8px;">↓</div>
        <div style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--rouaa-text-secondary); margin-bottom: 8px;">Source Document</div>
        <div style="color: var(--rouaa-text-muted); margin-bottom: 8px;">↓</div>
        <div style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--rouaa-text-secondary); margin-bottom: 8px;">Verified Fact</div>
        <div style="color: var(--rouaa-text-muted); margin-bottom: 8px;">↓</div>
        <div style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--rouaa-text-secondary); margin-bottom: 8px;">Financial Event</div>
        <div style="color: var(--rouaa-text-muted); margin-bottom: 8px;">↓</div>
        <div style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--rouaa-text-secondary); margin-bottom: 8px;">Evidence Record</div>
        <div style="color: var(--rouaa-text-muted); margin-bottom: 8px;">↓</div>
        <div style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--rouaa-text-secondary); margin-bottom: 8px;">Reasoning Trace</div>
        <div style="color: var(--rouaa-text-muted); margin-bottom: 8px;">↓</div>
        <div style="font-size: 16px; color: var(--rouaa-accent); font-weight: 600;">Institutional Decision Context</div>
      </div>
      <div class="text-center" style="margin-top: 32px;">
        <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--rouaa-text-muted); max-width: 560px; margin: 0 auto;">
          Market events are one example of intelligence inputs. The chain applies to any institutional decision supported by ROUAA. If a decision cannot be reconstructed through this chain, it was not a ROUAA-backed decision.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- ============ TRUST BOUNDARY ============ -->
  <section class="section" id="trust-boundary" style="background: var(--rouaa-bg-secondary);">
    <div class="container">
      <div style="max-width: 680px; margin: 0 auto; text-align: center; padding: 32px; background: var(--rouaa-surface); border: 1px solid var(--rouaa-accent-border); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); border-left: 4px solid var(--rouaa-accent);">
        <div style="font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--rouaa-accent); margin-bottom: 16px;">Where ROUAA Stops</div>
        <h2 style="margin-bottom: 16px;">Trust Boundary</h2>
        <p style="font-size: 15px; color: var(--rouaa-text-secondary); line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);">
          ROUAA provides evidence-backed intelligence infrastructure. Institutions retain responsibility for investment decisions, governance policies, approvals, and final actions.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="compliance">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header text-center" style="margin: 0 auto 48px;">
        <span class="eyebrow">Compliance Alignment</span>
        <h2>Built for governance, audit, and regulatory review.</h2>
        <p style="margin: 0 auto; max-width: 680px;">The Trust Framework is not certified against specific regulatory regimes — but it is architecturally aligned with what regulators, auditors, and investment committees require of institutional decision processes.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-4">
        <div class="card text-center">
          <h4 style="margin-bottom: 8px; color: var(--rouaa-accent);">Investment Committee</h4>
          <p style="font-size: 14px;">Research notes arrive with evidence chains. Committee can verify every claim in real time. Committees review conclusions together with the evidence supporting them.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card text-center">
          <h4 style="margin-bottom: 8px; color: var(--rouaa-accent);">Internal Audit</h4>
          <p style="font-size: 14px;">Every decision reconstructable. Every step logged. Every transformation documented. Audit processes gain clearer reconstruction paths and documented evidence chains.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card text-center">
          <h4 style="margin-bottom: 8px; color: var(--rouaa-accent);">Compliance &amp; Risk</h4>
          <p style="font-size: 14px;">Pre-trade and post-trade intelligence carry the same evidence chain. Risk review can interrogate the reasoning, not just the position.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card text-center">
          <h4 style="margin-bottom: 8px; color: var(--rouaa-accent);">Regulatory Review</h4>
          <p style="font-size: 14px;">When regulators ask "show me how you arrived at this" — the answer is one click. No reconstruction projects. No extended review cycles.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="text-center" style="margin-top: 32px;">
        <p style="font-size: 13px; color: var(--rouaa-text-muted); max-width: 560px; margin: 0 auto;">
          ROUAA is not certified to any specific regime (SOC 2, ISO 27001, etc.) at this stage. Certification programs address operational controls. The Trust Framework defines the intelligence governance model those controls operate within. Certification paths are evaluated as the company scales.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-section" style="background: var(--rouaa-bg-secondary);" id="cta">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Review the Trust Framework with our team.</h2>
      <p style="max-width: 640px; margin: 0 auto 32px;">
        Institutions are invited to review the Trust Framework in detail — including methodology papers, evidence chain samples, and governance rule documentation.
      </p>
